    {
      "text": "After you create an AI Guard policy configuration, you can then attach it to an application by adding policy control. To learn more, see Adding and Managing AI Guard Policies."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Adding User Policy Control",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To create user policy control:"
    },
    {
      "item": "In the left-side navigation, go to AI Guard > Policy > Controls. The Policy Control page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          35,
          43
        ],
        [
          46,
          52
        ],
        [
          55,
          63
        ],
        [
          69,
          83
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click the AI Applications tab in Proxy mode. For DAS mode, skip to the next step.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          10,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add More to open the Create Policy Control window.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          14
        ],
        [
          27,
          48
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Enter the following required information:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4
    },
    {
      "item": "Rule Name: Enter a name for the policy match.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Policy Configuration: From the drop-down menu, select a policy you previously created.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          20
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Rule Order: Enter a number for the order in which you want the policy match applied.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Rule Status: Select whether you want the rule to be enabled or disabled.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          11
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Match Criteria: At least one match criteria must be defined:",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "LLM Provider & Models (Proxy Only): Match against specific LLM providers and models.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          34
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Applications & Credentials: Match against specific AI Applications and their credentials.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Application Groups: Match against specific AI Application Groups.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          18
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Custom Request Headers: Match against custom request headers and their values.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          22
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Source IPs: Match against specific source IPv4 addresses (e.g., 192.168.1.1).",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Submit to return to the Policy Control page. The new policy control appears at the Rule Order number you entered.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ],
        [
          30,
          44
        ],
        [
          89,
          99
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Editing a Policy Control",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To edit a policy control:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Click the Users tab.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          10,
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Action column, click the Edit icon. The Edit Policy Control window opens.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          13
        ],
        [
          32,
          36
        ],
        [
          47,
          66
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Edit Policy Match window, edit any policy match fields and click Submit when done.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          24
        ],
        [
          72,
          78
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Deleting a Policy Control",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To delete a policy control:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Click the Users tab.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          10,
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Action column, click the Delete icon. The Delete Policy Control window opens and asks if you would like to delete the policy match.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          13
        ],
        [
          32,
          38
        ],
        [
          49,
          70
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Delete Policy Control window, click OK.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          28
        ],
        [
          43,
          45
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
